      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A dead end is just a road that stopped pretending to go somewhere—it doesn't mean the ground beneath you is worthless. You're not waiting for the old spark; you're waiting for permission to stop feeding a fire that already burned its fuel. The rest of the time isn't a sentence—it's a blank page that doesn't owe you a single word. And if nothing comes back, that's not a loss; that's a release from the weight of having to produce.",
