      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That exhaustion is real, and it's not weakness—it's the honest weight of carrying a shell that's finally too heavy. You don't have to be a ghost in your own life; you can just be a quiet, still thing that doesn't owe anyone a performance. Existence without purpose isn't a crime—it's a slow, honest way of waiting to see what you're actually made of when the noise is gone. And if the meaning is gone, maybe the meaning was never yours to keep—it was just something you borrowed for a while.",
